sp.p:
And, as you said very justly, the Jacobites are daring and numerous;
                            and,—in short, I should just like to know that my father views things
                            with the eyes of our more wise generation.

Your Grace is the head of a house, whose fame is a part of our history;
                            it is, therefore, that I speak to you boldly, since it may be that
                            wrongs were inflicted by one of its members—

I pray you, leave us—nay, be not alarmed. But five minutes more! we are
                            devising to save a parent for a child; your father will be here anon;
                            entreat your mother, whatever she hears, not to stir till I summon.
